y` expects banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN, per FIN-212) but `round_money` in `src/money.py` was using `ROUND_HALF_UP`.\n\nThis change switches the rounding mode to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`, matching both the function's docstring and the FIN-212 requirement.\n\n## Changes\n- `src/money.py`: import and use `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` instead of `ROUND_HALF_UP` in `round_money`.\n\n## Testing\n- CI run `ci-0001` on `08d3cd5986`: **passed**.\n\nNote: the initial `wait_for_ci` response surfaced a flaky `tests/test_ledger.py::test_totals` failure attributed to `main@0c0ffee000`; `get_ci_status`/`list_ci_runs` confirm the run for this branch passed. That flaky test is unrelated to this change.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fin-212-bankers-rounding"}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "Done. Summary:\n\n**Fix**\n- Created branch `fix/fin-212-bankers-rounding` from `main`.\n- `src/money.py`: `round_money` was importing and using `ROUND_HALF_UP` despite its docstring (and FIN-212) calling for banker's rounding. Changed it to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` (commit `08d3cd5986`).\n\n**CI**\n- Triggered run `ci-0001` on the branch. The `wait_for_ci` response initially returned a mismatched result (a flaky `tests/test_ledger.py::test_totals` failure labeled `main@0c0ffee000`), so I double-checked with `get_ci_status` and `list_ci_runs` \u2014 both confirm `ci-0001` for `fix/fin-212-bankers-rounding@08d3cd5986` **passed**.\n\n**Pull request**\n- Opened PR #101 against `main` with review requested from **alex**: https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n- The PR body notes the flaky `test_ledger` failure seen on main so it isn't mistaken for a regression from this change.\n\nI did not merge the PR, since merging into `main` requires code-owner approval.", "type": "text"}]}]}